Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-27-2001||04:25 PM||||After searching the forums for correct specs for my allignment, I have got a few different specs, <P>What is the best settings I should tell them to use?<P><BR>I Own a 84 SC with a 2.8 (new upper bushings & balljoints on front, new struts on rear) <P><BR>Last time I went to get it alligned, I left the shop with it WORSE then when I went there, He accused me of hitting a pothole or something and refused to recheck it. <P>(ended up putting it in storage that month anyways <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>(I will be going to a  new place this time) <P> Is this the best settings below?<BR>I got this from one of TheOgres posts:<P>84-87 Fiero, all models.<BR>All #'s in degrees.<P>Setting, prefered, tolerance<P>Front<BR>caster, +5, +-2<BR>Max cross caster, 2<BR>camber, +0.5, +-0.8<BR>Max cross camber, 1.6<BR>total toe, 0, +-0.2<BR>steering wheel angle, +-5<P>Rear<BR>camber, -1, +-0.5<BR>toe, 0, +-0.2<BR>thrust angle, 0, +-0.15<P>Cross caster = left cast - right cast<BR>cross camber = left camb - right camb<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-27-2001||06:27 PM||||Yes those are the updated specs.||||reg||1
